    <dc:description>Articles in this issue:

Elite Young Runners Are Becoming Freakishly Fast. Welcome to ‘Trackflation’

Streamer IShowSpeed Is Gen Z’s ESPN

I’m a Normie. Can Normies Really Vibe Code?

Arm’s CEO Insists the Market Needs His New CPU. It Could Piss Everyone Off

Our Favorite Brain-Boosting Toys for Kids of All Ages

Python Is So Slow. Can Julia Solve the Two-Language Problem?

Monica Lewinsky Has Always Hated Notifications

Quiz: Will AI Destroy Your Career?

14 New Tools for Taking on the Great Outdoors Properly

15 Design-Forward DIY Tools Worth Upgrading to This Year

Taylor Lorenz’s Screen Time Is Almost 17 Hours a Day

How Is Kalshi Not Gambling?

For $4,550, Would You Buy a Single Premium Watch or a Swarm of Affordable Ones?

Why Are Some Women Training for Pregnancy Like It’s a Marathon?

He Leaked the Secrets of a Southeast Asian Scam Compound. Then He Had to Get Out Alive

Why Minnesota Can’t Do More to Stop ICE

You’ve Never Heard of China’s Greatest Sci-Fi Novel

Thousands of Companies Are Driving China’s AI Boom. A Government Registry Tracks Them All

Your First Humanoid Robot Coworker Will Probably Be Chinese

China’s AI Boyfriend Business Is Taking On a Life of Its Own

China’s Renewable Energy Revolution Is a Huge Mess That Might Save the World

She Was Given Up by Her Chinese Parents—and Spent 14 Years Trying to Find a Way Back

He Went to Prison for Gene-Editing Babies. Now He’s Planning to Do It Again

How China’s ‘Crystal Capital’ Cornered the Market on a Western Obsession

Chinese EV Batteries Are Eating the World

Trump Declared a Space Race With China. The US Is Losing

True Patriots Are Cashing In on the Apocalypse

Scientists Thought Parkinson’s Was in Our Genes. It Might Be in the Water

A New Anonymous Phone Carrier Lets You Sign Up With Nothing but a Zip Code

Want This Hearing Aid? Well, Who Do You Know?

Ruby Is Not a Serious Programming Language

OpenAI's Fidji Simo Plans to Make ChatGPT Way More Useful—and Have You Pay For It

All of My Employees Are AI Agents, and So Are My Executives

Alex Karp Goes to War

How KPop Demon Hunters Star EJAE Topped the Charts

Ed Zitron Gets Paid to Love AI. He Also Gets Paid to Hate AI

The Cure

The Future of AI Isn’t Just Slop

Parents Fell in Love With Alpha School’s Promise. Then They Wanted Out

Why AI Breaks Bad

Programming in Assembly Is Brutal, Beautiful, and Maybe Even a Path to Better AI

Gear for Good: 20 Eco-Friendly Items That Score a Win for the Planet—and for You

The Real Stakes, and Real Story, of Peter Thiel’s Antichrist Obsession

The Story of DOGE, as Told by Federal Workers

The 22 Very Online Upstarts Changing the Face of Politics

She Fought the Far Right Online for Years. Now She Wants to Do It in Congress

I Thought I Knew Silicon Valley. I Was Wrong

Elon Musk Is Out to Rule Space. Can Anyone Stop Him?

One Vigilante, 22 Cell Tower Fires, and a World of Conspiracies

The Superyacht, the Billionaire, and a Wildly Improbable Disaster at Sea

The Baby Died. Whose Fault Is It?

What It’s Like Watching Dozens of Bodies Decompose (for Science)

Why Did a $10 Billion Startup Let Me Vibe-Code for Them—and Why Did I Love It?

AI Isn’t Coming for Hollywood. It's Already Arrived

Lisa Su Runs AMD—and Is Out for Nvidia’s Blood

Psychedelic Therapy Crashed and Burned. MAHA Might Bring It Back

Life Without Screens: This Camp Is a Teen’s Worst Nightmare

A Head-to-Toe Breakdown of Social Media’s Billion-Dollar Remedies

Wired is a full-color monthly American magazine, published in both print and online editions, that reports on how emerging technologies affect culture, the economy and politics. Monthly edition, best run at the start of every month.</dc:description>
